{sov: Notes}
JGB Arrangement: Transformed J.J. Cale's laid-back original (and Eric Clapton's
hit) into an upbeat, high-energy reggae-funk jam featured on 'Cats Under the Stars'.

Main Riff Movement: Built around the quick-passing 2-bar loop of C - Eb - F - C.
The Eb to F movement creates the signature bouncing chromatic jump.

Reggae Skank Strumming: Accent the offbeats (and 'and' of every beat) with tight,
short upstrokes on top-three string triad voicings.

Solo Section: Often extended for long, fluid improvs. Jerry typically navigates
the changes using C Major Pentatonic and C Mixolydian with fast chromatic lead-ins.
{eov}